+# Corpus fetching
+
+The repository records that the corpus files were fetched raw from
+`raw.githubusercontent.com`. It also records that `grep.app` was used to locate the
+public `CLAUDE.md` and `AGENTS.md` files; `grep.app` was a discovery service, not a
+file-download mirror.
+
+No evidence in this checkout records the per-domain rate limit actually encountered:
+the number of visits allowed, the length of the accounting window, and the cooldown
+after a breach are all unknown. The checkout likewise does not identify any CDN or
+mirror host used to download files other than `raw.githubusercontent.com`. These
+values and hosts are intentionally not inferred from current provider documentation,
+because that would not establish what this corpus fetch actually hit.
